# Coding Standards (Frontend)

- Use TypeScript strictly; no implicit `any`.
- Prefer standalone components and Angular Signals for state.
- Keep services thin over `HttpClient`; use typed DTOs for all API I/O.
- Handle loading and error states explicitly (visible indicators + messages).
- Follow SOLID; keep features isolated and modular.
- Generate production-ready code.
- Prefer clear intent over cleverness; only comment non-obvious intent.

## Naming
- Components: `PascalCase` class, `kebab-case` files (`pos-cart.component.ts`).
- Services: `SomethingService`; DTOs mirror backend names (`OrderDto`).
